        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "```\nTROPICAL RAINFOREST — VERTICAL STRUCTURE"
    },
    {
      "id": "06-TROPICAL-TREES.md#004",
      "path": [
        "06-TROPICAL-TREES.md"
      ],
      "level": 0,
      "line": 1,
      "metadata": {
        "backsource_ids": "[proof-backfill:dendrology:06-tropical-trees, git-history:dendrology:06-tropical-trees]",
        "canonical_path": "dendrology/06-TROPICAL-TREES.md",
        "concepts": "[tropical, trees]",
        "current_path": "dendrology/06-TROPICAL-TREES.md",
        "id": "maxim:dendrology:tropical-trees",
        "index_roles": "[guide, root-concept]",
        "kind": "guide",
        "maxim_schema": "maxim.frontmatter.v1",
        "module": "dendrology",
        "remap_from": "[]",
        "remap_to": "[]",
        "root_concepts": "[tropical, trees]",
        "section": "dendrology",
        "source_custody": "partial",
        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "Tropical Tree Diversity: Rainforest Structure, Emergents, Epiphytes",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "Height\n  50m+  +-[EMERGENT LAYER]------+   Giant isolated crowns above main canopy\n        | Exposed; wind-pollinated|   Dipterocarps, Brazil nut, Emergent figs\n        | or animal-dispersed    |   Crown fire does not spread to this height\n        | seeds; thermally       |   Rain initiates mass synchronized flowering\n        | extreme conditions     |\n  30m   +-[MAIN CANOPY]----------+   Continuous leaf surface; 90%+ of light\n        | Closed or near-closed  |   Main interception layer; temperature\n        | canopy; major habitat  |   stable; wind-buffered; dense shade below\n        | for birds + epiphytes  |\n  15m   +-[UNDERSTORY]-----------+   Sub-canopy tree species (palms, tree ferns)\n        | Deep shade <5% full sun|   Adapted: large leaves, horizontal spread\n        | Diffuse, filtered light|   High humidity, low VPD\n        |                        |\n  5m    +-[SHRUB LAYER]----------+   Dense forbs and shrubs in disturbed patches\n        | Ferns, palms, shrubs   |   Low diversity in deep shade\n        | Often sparse in intact |\n        | closed canopy forest   |\n  0m    +-[FOREST FLOOR]---------+   Rapid litter decomposition (warm + humid)\n        | Thin A horizon; roots  |   Surface roots; mycorrhizal mat\n        | concentrated at surface|   Very few ground-layer plants in dense shade\n```"
    },
