        "source_custody": "partial",
        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "Tropical Tree Diversity: Rainforest Structure, Emergents, Epiphytes",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "Buttress roots are plank-like lateral extensions from the trunk base, radiating outward across the soil surface. They are ecologically diagnostic of tropical lowland forest."
    },
    {
