        "title": "Tropical Tree Diversity: Rainforest Structure, Emergents, Epiphytes",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "**Why buttress roots exist:**\n1. **Mechanical stability hypothesis**: Shallow soils (oxisols, ultisols) provide poor anchorage for deep tap roots. Buttresses spread the load over a wider area, increasing stability against wind throw in large-crowned emergents.\n2. **Nutrient acquisition hypothesis**: Buttresses extend root surface area into the nutrient-rich O/A horizon where litter decomposes, effectively enlarging the foraging area for P and K.\n3. Both hypotheses have supporting evidence; likely both are true."
    },
    {
